There's no search input in this directory (it's a config dir, no app code), so here's the vanilla version to drop in; nothing was edited or run.

```js
const input = document.querySelector('#search');
let timer, controller;

input.addEventListener('input', () => {
  clearTimeout(timer);
  timer = setTimeout(async () => {
    controller?.abort(); // drop the stale in-flight request so old results can't overwrite new ones
    controller = new AbortController();
    try {
      const res = await fetch(`/api/search?q=${encodeURIComponent(input.value)}`, { signal: controller.signal });
      render(await res.json());
    } catch (e) {
      if (e.name !== 'AbortError') throw e;
    }
  }, 300);
});
```

Swap `#search`, `/api/search` and `render` for your own names.

In React, the same thing goes in an effect:

```js
useEffect(() => {
  const controller = new AbortController();
  const timer = setTimeout(() => search(query, controller.signal), 300);
  return () => { clearTimeout(timer); controller.abort(); };
}, [query]);
```

Here `search` must pass the signal to `fetch` and ignore `AbortError`.

